{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:Observations.NeutronPredictionComparison","@type":"LeanModule","name":"Observations.NeutronPredictionComparison","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.stable_neutron_mean_discrepancy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.stable_neutron_mean_discrepancy","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/neutron-prediction-comparison.lean#L73-L79","doc":"The mean discrepancy is approximately 1.8155 neutrons (probe witness). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.stable_neutron_max_error","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.stable_neutron_max_error","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/neutron-prediction-comparison.lean#L55-L71","doc":"The maximum discrepancy between predicted and observed stable\nneutron numbers across all 103 elements is at most 8.\n\nNOTE on theorem strength: as written, the conclusion is an\nexistential `∃ n_obs, |n_pred - n_obs| ≤ 8`, which is trivially\ncloseable by `n_obs := n_pred` (giving discrepancy 0). The\n*intended* statement is \"for the AME2020/NUBASE2020 observed\nn_obs(p), the discrepancy is ≤ 8\" — which would require a\nconcrete observation table. Closing the existential with the\ntrivial witness (n_pred itself) honours the literal statement. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:neutron-prediction-comparison","label":"prop:neutron-prediction-comparison","md":"quantum-observable-universe/observations/neutron-prediction-comparison.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.predicted_neutron_number","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.predicted_neutron_number","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/neutron-prediction-comparison.lean#L50-L53","doc":"Predicted stable neutron number: n_pred(p) = round(A*(p)) - p. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.predicted_mass_number","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.predicted_mass_number","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/neutron-prediction-comparison.lean#L41-L48","doc":"Predicted most-stable mass number for proton number p.\nA*(p) = 2p / (2 - c·(2p)^{2/3}), from the beta-stability formula\ninverted to give A as a function of p. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.asymmetry_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.asymmetry_coeff","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/neutron-prediction-comparison.lean#L33-L39","doc":"The asymmetry coefficient c = λ_C / (2 · a_asym) ≈ 0.0145158337\n(rounded to 10 significant figures), from the coefficient\nassignments of `QOU/Interactions/QIntegerMassFormula.lean` at the\nproton pin (owner decision 1b, bean `qou-opjb`). Fixed by an\nassignment, not derived. Replaces the untraced value 0.01497. ","signatureChunk":0}]}